WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.710
Once one of the funniest men in Hollywood,
these days Vince Vaughn struggles to find

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.370
laughs on the big screen.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:12.800
What got the star of Swingers and Wedding
Crashers stuck in a career rut?

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.800
Flops

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.480
Vaughn's Hollywood dry spell may have to do
with the fact that his last few movies have

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.480
tanked.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:24.570
With dismal reviews, 2016's Unfinished Business—about
three coworkers who embark on a European business

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:29.700
trip gone terribly wrong—made headlines
for its shockingly low box-office returns.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:35.980
According to Box Office Mojo, the film grossed
just $4.7 million in its opening weekend to

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.370
become the worst-performing major release
of Vaughn's career.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:44.780
The fact that it finished its theatrical run
with about $10.2 million against a $35 million

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:46.860
budget only looked worse.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.921
Unfinished Business followed four other flops:
The Internship, The Watch, The Dilemma, and

00:00:51.921 --> 00:00:53.060
Delivery Man.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:57.960
And only Delivery Man managed to earn a profit
on its domestic box office...and only because

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.630
it was so cheap to make in the first place.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:01.870
Ouch.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.489
True Defective

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:07.310
When Vaughn agreed to star in HBO's second
season of True Detective, he may have been

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.280
aware that his career was in a rut.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.440
The show's critically acclaimed first season
was a highlight for Matthew McConaughey's

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.440
in 2013.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.070
If it worked for him, it could work for Vaughn,
right?

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:22.180
Of course, now we know that True Detective
season two couldn't live up to its predecessor.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.490
And Vaughn's performance didn't help much.

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:29.190
Whether he was threatening characters or reciting
one of the series' notorious monologues, he

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.350
looked out of place and out of his depth.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:35.250
By the end of the season, it mainly served
to remind us that Vaughn is only fun to watch

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.710
when the laughs are intentional.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.390
Casting Confusion

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:43.990
For years after Wedding Crashers, Vaughn struggled
to find his footing in Hollywood, often choosing

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:45.770
roles that felt very out of place.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:50.120
There was the awkward attempt at becoming
a romantic leading man, like in 2006's The

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.120
Break-Up.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.040
Two years later, Vaughn starred opposite Reese
Witherspoon in Four Christmases.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.170
In both cases, Vaughn's style of humor didn't
match the rest of the movies.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.720
Fans longed to see him in the dude-friendly
movies that made him popular.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.300
What they got was Couples Retreat and Fred
Claus.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.670
Ho ho no.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:10.819
Getting older

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:15.379
When your career is defined by frat-boy movies
like Swingers, Old School, and Wedding Crashers,

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:18.120
eventually, you get too old to play those
parts.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.650
Now in his 40s, Vaughn has officially entered
that territory.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:26.129
The only time that he should be on a college
campus is to take one of his kids on a tour.

00:02:26.129 --> 00:02:28.419
Speaking of...

00:02:28.419 --> 00:02:29.419
Family man

00:02:29.419 --> 00:02:32.499
Another reason he may not be a top dog in
Hollywood anymore?

00:02:32.499 --> 00:02:36.189
Vaughn's actually been married to Canadian
realtor Kyla Weber for several years.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:40.200
They have two children together: daughter
Locklyn and son Vernon.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.620
It's possible that Vaughn has slowed his pace
to focus on being a husband and a dad.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.569
After over 30 years in the business, he may
be tired of the grind.

00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:53.019
Plus, with a reported net worth of $50 million,
he's not in danger of being unable to provide

00:02:53.019 --> 00:02:54.379
for his family.

00:02:54.379 --> 00:02:57.120
And maybe fatherhood will inspire his new
direction.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.049
The right Pixar project may be all it takes
for a family-friendly version of Vince Vaughn

00:03:01.049 --> 00:03:03.269
to mount the brilliant comeback we're all
waiting for.

00:03:03.269 --> 00:03:05.709
It seems to be working for Owen Wilson...

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:06.719
Thanks for watching!

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.670
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:13.239
And leave us a comment to let us know how
you think Vince Vaughn can start swinging

00:03:13.239 --> 00:03:13.629
again...

